-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",419,{
[13377]="70017921\n1\tTalk to Huldar\tThe Rune-keeper Huldar is at Othrikar, in the North Downs. You have been told that the dwarf Huldar may be able to teach you about beneficial runes of healing.\n2\tTalk to Huldar and assist in the defence of Othrikar\tHuldar is at Othrikar, in the North Downs. The dwarf Huldar has agreed to teach you what he knows about runes of healing if you help repel an attack by the Dourhands.\n3\tTalk to Huldar at Othrikar\tHuldar is at Othrikar, in the North Downs. You were of great assistance to the dwarves of Othrikar during the Dourhand attack and should speak now to Huldar as was agreed.\n",
[13378]="70057183\n1\tTalk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n2\tComplete the quest \"Chopping Wood\"\030Complete the quest \"Catching Chickens\"\030Complete the quest \"Picking Berries\"\tGrimbeorn's three tasks can be found in and around the Beorninghús as well as close by in the Beorninglands. You should complete the three tasks that Grimbeorn has asked you to complete.\n3\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
[13379]="7002F922\n1\tCollect pelts from Norcrofts pack-wolves\tNorcrofts pack-wolves reside in and around Âmbal's den, west of Caddabrand's camp. Collecting the fine hides of pack-wolves is sure to be rewarded by the opportunistic Caddabrand.\n2\tCollect pelts from Norcrofts pack-wolves (total: 10)\tNorcrofts pack-wolves reside in and around Âmbal's den, west of Caddabrand's camp. Collecting the fine hides of pack-wolves is sure to be rewarded by the opportunistic Caddabrand.\n3\tBring the wolf-pelts to Caddabrand\tCaddabrand's camp lies east of Âmbal's den, a ways south of the river-crossing. Caddabrand should be pleased to see the initiative you have taken in collecting him these tradeable wolf-hides.\n",
[13380]="7000850F\n1\tFind the hunter Machan\tMachan the hunter should be somewhere in the region of Sálgaitë to the south-east. The hunter Murdaigán has asked you to locate Machan, who was hunting fire-worms in Malenhad.\n",
[13381]="70008B88\n1\tTalk to Ormulf Worm-hunter\tOrmulf Worm-hunter is at Othrikar, far to the west in the north-central North Downs. Sigrun has seen from afar that the keep of Helegrod appears to be crawling with worms and drakes and has asked you to consult with Ormulf Worm-hunter about what must be done.\n",
[13382]="70015E06\n1\tBring the note to Calelloth at Gwingris\030Defeat Arzgât and search his body\tArzgât dwells near a small range of mountains, on the hillside of Carchres south of the road to Rivendell, east of Gwingris. Calelloth has instructed you to go forth and defeat the half-orc Arzgât.\n",
[13383]="70015E2A\n1\tDefeat Brunanc\tThe worm-eggs belonging to the spawn of Brunanc lie upon the hillsides south-east of Gwingris. Daegennan has asked you to destroy the eggs of the worms to draw forth their leader, Brunanc.\n2\tTalk to Daegennan at Gwingris\tDaegennan is at Gwingris, north-west of Brunanc's nest. You should return to Daegennan with news of your victory.\n",
[13384]="70034D22\n1\tPonds can be found near Thrymm's Camp in the north-eastern Writhendowns. You should investigate the effects of the cold and snow around the frozen ponds of the Writhendowns.\t\n2\tSpeak with Thrymm Red-beard\tThis situation appears more dire than originally thought. Thrymm Red-beard will be waiting back at his camp.\n",
[13385]="70068366\n1\tSpeak with Zerkho\030Speak with Karbah\030Speak with Mallax\tYou were instructed to consult with the experts in the camp to learn about the animals that you would hunt across the crags and moors in the eastern Cape of Umbar. They can be found in the encampment.\n2\tSpeak with Abido\tYou should now have an understanding of how the people of Umbar will use the various items gained from a hunt in the crags and moors of the Cape of Umbar. Return to Abido and speak with him.\n",
[13386]="70067D9D\n1\tWait a moment\tAnyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures.\n2\tSummon Anyâmat with the whistle and complete 'Fightin' Freebooters'\tAnyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures. While in Zamarzîr, use Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory to summon Anyâmat to your side.\n3\tSummon Anyâmat with the whistle and complete 'What if We Fight a Giant Crab?'\030Summon Anyâmat with the whistle and complete 'Zamarzîr Treasure Hunt'\tAnyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures. While in Zamarzîr, use Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory to summon Anyâmat to your side.\n4\tSummon Anyâmat with the whistle and talk to her\tAnyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures.\n",
[13387]="7004146B\n1\tSearch for a bucket near the mere outside Roamingstar's glade\tA bucket can be found on the banks of the Gilrain in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Roamingstar has asked you to aid her in healing the lands of Dor-en-Ernil by using the waters of the Gilrain.\n2\tHeal war-torn earth near Roamingstar's glade (total: 6)\tWar-torn earth can be found in and around Roamingstar's glade. Roamingstar has asked you to aid her in healing the lands of Dor-en-Ernil.\n3\tTalk to Roamingstar\tRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have healed the earth wounded by the war in Gondor and should now return to Roamingstar.\n",
[13388]="70045FE5\n1\tDismantle the first set of barricades (total: 2)\tThe first set of barricades are located just inside the front gates of Minas Tirith.\n2\tDismantle the second set of barricades (total: 2)\tThe second set of barricades are located in front of the entrance to the southern end of the First Circle of Minas Tirith.\n3\tDismantle the final set of barricades (total: 2)\tThe last set of barricades are located just in front of the ramp to the Second Circle in the southern end of Minas Tirith's First Circle.\n4\tSpeak with Imrahil\tImrahil can be found outside the gates to Minas Tirith. You should speak with Imrahil.\n",
[13389]="70027F88\n1\tWounded townsfolk of the Stag-clan can be found in various parts of Lhan Tarren. You should quickly heal the wounded villagers, before another life is lost to the horrible attack that took place in Trum Dreng.\t\n2\tTell Elain that you have helped to heal the wounded townsfolk\tElain is in Lhan Tarren. You should return to Elain to see what else can be done to help right this terrible wrong.\n",
[13390]="700490DA\n1\tExamine the chamber of Narchraw again\tBarad-dûr is located in eastern Dor Amarth. You should examine the chamber of Narchraw again.\n2\tInspect the chamber door\tBarad-dûr is located in eastern Dor Amarth. You should examine the chamber of Narchraw again.\n3\tEscape Barad-dûr\030Defeat Glúrugoth's guards (total: 6)\tEscape Barad-dûr and fight off Glúrugoth's guards.\n4\tTalk to Lômazar\tLômazar can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth. You should speak with Lômazar.\n",
[13391]="7004DA36\n1\tSpread healing salve on scarred trees (total: 10)\tScarred trees can be found near Tholkát in Eryn Lasgalen. You should heal scarred trees with the salve given to you by Thranduil.\n2\tTalk to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You should talk to Thranduil.\n",
[13392]="70066B4A\n1\tDiscover the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor\tDefeating Corsairs at the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor may help peace find these shores once more sooner rather than later.\n2\tDefeat Corsairs at the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor (total: 10)\tDefeating Corsairs at the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor may help peace find these shores once more sooner rather than later.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of Corsairs at the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor.\n",
[13393]="7001A636\n1\tTalk to Nífdir at his camp\tNífdir can be found at a small camp to the west of Estolad Mernael. Nenedhel has asked you once again to seek out Nífdir in the heart of the Drownholt.\n2\tApproach Mirk-huorns (total: 5)\tHuorns can be found in Sâd Meryrn, due south of Nífdir's small camp. You should travel north and west to reach their glade. You should approach Huorns and attempt to speak with them, but Nífdir has advised you to be prepared for much open hostility.\n3\tApproach the largest Mirk-huorn and attempt to speak with it\tThe Wrathful Huorn stands in Sâd Meryrn. One Mirk-huorn does not seem as malicious as the rest; you should approach it and learn what you can from it.\n4\tTalk to Nífdir at his camp\tNífdir is at the camp overlooking Sâd Meryrn from the north. You should speak with Nífdir and tell him of the strange conversation of sorts that passed between yourself and the Mirk-huorn.\n",
[13394]="70024BB3\n1\tVisit Ona Kay, the Eating Contest Announcer\tThe Eating Contest begins at Ona Kay, the first Announcer.\n2\tSpeak with the mayor of Winter-home about the festivities\tThe mayor and his wife, hosts of the Yule Festivities, are in the centre of the celebration. You should speak with the mayor about the various events of the festival, for he wishes to greet all who arrive.\n3\tSpeak with the mayor's wife\tThe mayor's wife is standing near the mayor, Winston Goodnough, watching over the festivities. The mayor's wife wishes to speak with you.\n4\tSpeak with someone from Winter-home to continue your tour\tYou should find your next destination on your tour of the town. Maybe one of the helpful servants knows what you should look at next?\n5\tSpeak with Cecil Voller at the Snowball Field\tCecil Voller is at the Snowball Field, north of the town.\n6\tSpeak with the hobbit-announcer about the Theatre Event\tThe hobbit-announcer of the travelling theatre can be found in Winter-home. You should speak with the hobbit-announcer about the Theatre event.\n7\tExplore the other corner of Winter-home, for it looks interesting\tIt seems you've not explored the south-west corner of the town; you should explore it before returning to the mayor....\n8\tSpeak with the man near Gareth Rust; he seems to have something to say\tA man standing near Gareth Rust beckons you. You should speak with the man near Gareth Rust.\n9\tReturn to Mayor Goodnough to finish your tour\tMayor Goodnough is in the centre of town. You should return to Mayor Goodnough now that you have finished your tour of Winter-home's many events.\n",
[13395]="7005A73F\n1\tGather gems (total: 12)\tGather gems.\n2\tBring the gems to Zádokh Flint-eye at Zidir-nesad\tZidir-nesad, The Steepset is located in Máttugard. You should bring the gems to Zádokh Flint-eye at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset.\n",
[13396]="70067CAD\n1\tSearch the shore of the islands south-west for the Temámir ship\tBekhel enlisted you to search for signs of the Temámir ship near the settlement of Halrax. You recall the bond you made to keep their motivation secret.\n2\tSpeak with the dwarf\tWhile searching for the Temámir vessel, you discovered a wounded Temámir sailor stranded on the shore.\n3\tFind the Corsair ship beached on the shore\tMulûg sent you toward the Corsair ship that set upon his vessel and stole the shipment bound for Umbar Baharbêl.\n4\tFace the Corsair captain\tYou found the Corsair's ship. You also found the captain. Confront him and find the cargo.\n5\tBoard the Corsair ship and search the deck\tYou can see nothing that looks like a shipment on the shore. Perhaps the cargo you seek is on the deck.\n6\tCollect the Temámir cargo\tWith the captain dispatched and his crew eliminated the cargo is yours.\n7\tSpeak with Bekhel near the Corsair's ship\tBekhel and his entourage arrived while you fought the captain. You hear them on the shore nearby.\n8\tSpeak with Ithurga at his home in Halrax\tBekhel thanked you for your assistance in recovering the stolen shipment and dispatched you to Halrax to inform Ithurga that Halrax is beyond suspicion and well-liked by the Kindred of the Coins.\n",
[13397]="70027B10\n1\tFind and challenge Gluthrak, Hoital, or Farmak\tThe Uruk-hai named Gluthrak, Hoital, and Farmak can be found somewhere within the Ring of Isengard. Morflak's lackey wants you to fight one of the Uruk-hai named by his boss in order to quell any challenges to his power.\n2\tTalk to Morflak's lackey\tMorflak's lackey has some more names for you.\n3\tFind and challenge Matum, Urbhár, or Golb\tThe Uruk-hai named Matum, Urbhár, and Golb can be found somewhere within the Ring of Isengard.\n4\tTalk to Morflak's lackey\tMorflak's lackey is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[13398]="70002E25\n1\tEnvenom the spiders' egg-sacs\tEgg-sacs of both the Trapdoor and Flesh-gnawer broods may be found in the Wovenvales, in the north-west corner of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp. You should use the fangs you collected to envenom the egg-sacs of the Wovenvale spiders.\n2\tStab Trapdoor egg-sacs with Flesh-gnawer fangs (quantity: see journal)\030Stab Flesh-gnawer egg-sacs with Trapdoor fangs (quantity: see journal)\tEgg-sacs of both the Trapdoor and Flesh-gnawer broods may be found in the Wovenvales, in the north-west corner of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp. You should use the fangs you collected to envenom the egg-sacs of the Wovenvale spiders.\n",
[13399]="70009823\n1\tFind the solution to the riddle\tThe treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed: \"The end of your search lies at the beginning. My treasure was always there, but you did not see.\" You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.\n2\tBring the mouldy book to Culang\tCulang is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, west of the cross-roads of Canadiach. You found a hollow compartment in the stone marker that you believed to mark the location of the treasure and recovered a mouldy book from the hidden space. You should bring this book to Culang.\n",
[13400]="700533E8\n1\tExamine George\tYou think that perhaps it is time to escape Farmer Sandson's coop.\n",
[13401]="700533EC\n1\tTravel to The Carrock\tThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.\n2\tFind the Beorninghús\tThe Vales of Anduin is a lovely place.\n3\tGet to Lake Town!\tThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.\n4\tTravel to Erebor, the Lonely Mountain\tThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.\n5\tSit on the throne under the mountain\tErebor is a lovely place.\n",
[13402]="70028B5A\n1\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund in Thror's Coomb in Enedwaith. Ariene found a powerful weapon in the hills of Enedwaith and believes Frithgeir may know where to find more.\n",
[13403]="7000D1A7\n1\tTalk to Barthavron\tBarthavron is in the market square of the Falathlorn homestead. Barchiril has sent you to speak with her friend Barthavron.\n",
[13404]="70016B21\n1\tSmash deep-worm eggs in Tanunshush (total: 8)\tThe deep-worms keep their eggs at Tanunshush, north-west of The Cross-roads of Ash, north of The Burning Stair. The population of deep-worms needs to be kept in check by destroying their eggs.\n2\tTalk to Ölfun at the Cross-roads of Ash\tÖlfun is at the Cross-roads of Ash, south-east of Tanunshush. Ölfun will want to know that you smashed many deep-worm eggs, contributing to lowering the population of deep-worms in the Flaming Deeps.\n",
[13405]="7001BF9B\n1\tDeliver the dwarf pick-axes to Henir at Iorvinas\030Collect dwarf pick-axes (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found within Iorvinas. Henir believes that there is something of value within the ruins where he hides. He does not think that the Orcs can get the materials on their own and wants to know if the Dourhands are providing them with tools needed for their work.\n",
[13406]="7003FF1D\n1\tFind and defeat the traitor\tThe traitor is likely hanging around near the Great Hall.\n",
[13407]="7000D1A6\n1\tTalk to Rambi\tRambi is in the market square within the Thorin's Hall homestead. Rúni has told you to speak with his friend Rambi about acquiring goods for your house.\n",
[13408]="7000D1A8\n1\tTalk to Rolf Bracegirdle\tRolf Bracegirdle is in the market square in the Michel Delving homestead. Andy Brockhouse has asked you to speak with Rolf Bracegirdle, a decorator who might be able to help you furnish your home.\n",
})
